+# Baoji
+
+## Telemetry
+
+- Terrain: Located at the western end of the Guanzhong Plain, Baoji is crossed by the Wei River and hemmed in by the Qinling Mountains to the south and loess tablelands to the north; the urban area stretches in a belt along the Wei River valley.
+- Step: Located on China's second terrain step, in the transition zone between the Qinling Mountains and the Wei River Plain, with terrain descending from south to north.
+- Climate: Warm-temperate, semi-humid continental monsoon climate with four distinct seasons, hot rainy summers, and cold dry winters; representative urban elevation is about 600 metres.
+- Challenge: Midsummer heat, humid river-valley air, and short intense rainfall place sustained demands on vehicle cooling, energy management, and equipment waterproofing.
+
